From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Portal maintainers <portal@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] opengl: accept CRLF shader resource lines

The ARM64 KWin source is staged through Portal's Windows build workspace.
Normalize the trailing carriage return before matching KWin's embedded GLSL
include directives so the current Forky shader resources are expanded before
Mesa compiles them.

This is limited to shader preprocessing and does not change the renderer or
graphics backend selection.
---
 src/opengl/glshader.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/opengl/glshader.cpp b/src/opengl/glshader.cpp
--- a/src/opengl/glshader.cpp
+++ b/src/opengl/glshader.cpp
@@ -112,7 +112,10 @@ std::optional<QByteArray> GLShader::preprocess(const QByteArray &src, GLenum sha
 
     for (auto it = split.begin(); it != split.end(); it++) {
-        const auto &line = *it;
+        QByteArray line = *it;
+        if (line.endsWith('\r')) {
+            line.chop(1);
+        }
         if (line.startsWith("#version")) {
             // this is intentionally ignored!
        } else if (line.startsWith("#include \"") && line.endsWith("\"")) {
            static constexpr ssize_t includeLength = QByteArrayView("#include \"").size();
-- 
